      "writtenOn": "2025-10-21T17:43:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no deferred execution here. `ExecuteGLWork` will execute the lambda immediately, hence we don\u0027t need to care about the lifetime here.\n\nThis might sound unnecessary, why do we need to use `ExecuteGLWork`? Corentin and I discussed and the plan is that in future, all code won\u0027t be able to call `GetGL` directly. They will have to get the gl function pointers indirectly via `AddGLWork`/`ExecuteGLWork`\u0027s lambda.",
      "parentUuid": "87cc0696_065490cf",
